# Security

Portfolio is mostly static — focus on **contact form abuse**, **secret handling**, and **safe external links**.

## Secrets

- Never commit `.env`, API keys, or SMTP credentials
- Provide `.env.example` with placeholder values only
- Backend secrets: `RESEND_API_KEY`, `CONTACT_TO_EMAIL`, `EMAIL_FROM` — server only
- Frontend: only `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` vars; no email API keys in client

## Contact Form

- Rate limit: `@nestjs/throttler` on `POST /contact` — see `nestjs-api.mdc`
- Honeypot field hidden from users — reject if populated
- Max body lengths enforced in DTO
- Sanitize output in emails — no HTML injection from user message (escape or plain text)
- CORS: whitelist site origin(s) only

## Headers (NestJS)

- `helmet()` enabled
- Production: HTTPS only behind reverse proxy

## Frontend

- External links: `rel="noopener noreferrer"` on `target="_blank"`
- No `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` unless MDX pipeline sanitizes content
- MDX: disallow raw `<script>`, `<iframe>`, event handlers in user content
- Resume PDF in `public/` — no sensitive data beyond public resume content

## Dependencies

- Run `npm audit` periodically; patch high/critical before deploy
- Pin major versions in lockfile; review new packages before adding

## Logging

- Do not log contact form message bodies in production
- Do not log env vars at startup beyond "configured/not configured"

## Do Not

- Add admin panel or database without auth hardening plan
- Expose internal error details to API clients
- Store contact submissions in DB without encryption/at-rest plan — email-only is fine for v1
